Added `Record::from_bytes` in [record.rs](src/record.rs#L24-L35), verified with a throwaway test (compact and whitespace-padded rows both parsed correctly), then removed the test.

```rust
pub fn from_bytes(bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<Self, csv::Error> {
    let mut reader = csv::ReaderBuilder::new()
        .has_headers(false)
        .trim(csv::Trim::All)
        .from_reader(bytes);

    let mut record = csv::ByteRecord::new();
    reader.read_byte_record(&mut record)?;
    record.deserialize(None)
}
```

It reads a single CSV row from a raw byte slice — no header row, columns matched positionally in `type,client,tx,amount` order — with the same `Trim::All` whitespace handling `load_records` uses on the full file, so a row sliced out via the mmap index parses identically to one read through the normal streaming path.

The 5 build warnings are all pre-existing from the in-progress `IndexBuffer`/`client.rs` wiring (unused imports, an unused `index_mmap` param, `get`/`set` not yet called) — none of them are new from this change.

